Daily animals is a realtime noise visualisation that changes based on the time of the day. It tries to critique the rituals daily routine forces upon us as a shared system and how that affects the city.

The noise amplitudes were programmed by logging the traffic on the roads. This helped in telling stories around ritualisation within the city. Made at Media Lab de Prado, Madrid.
